      },
      "titleX": 97,
      "titleY": 137,
      "body": "An answer is rarely the end of the process.\nWhen something seems obvious, I want to understand what makes it so: the patterns, connections, and assumptions beneath it. I tend to follow a question further, especially when something does not quite add up. Curiosity, for me, is a way of looking closer and questioning what seems certain.\nUranus offers a fitting parallel. Beneath its seemingly simple atmosphere lies a complex interior unlike that of the planets we know best. Perhaps the most interesting answers are things that are hidden beneath what first appears obvious, waiting to be understood.",
