    {
      "key": "ban-sung",
      "route": "/community/ban-sung",
      "frameId": "26:2",
      "title": {
        "path": "community/type/ban-sung-title.svg",
        "text": "Ban Sung Project",
        "width": 548,
        "height": 58,
        "offsetX": 3.2160000801086426,
        "offsetY": 8.903998374938965,
        "artWidth": 544.0,
        "artHeight": 47.0
      },
      "titleX": 213,
      "titleY": 132,
      "body": "Bản Sưng is a Dao community in Hòa Bình, northern Vietnam, where I joined the Bản Sưng Project and worked alongside local villagers to repair 2 km of mountain roads, contributing to safer access and essential community infrastructure. I also spent time with 30+ local households, taking part in cultural exchanges and learning through hands-on experiences such as making Dó paper, dyeing indigo, and exploring the community’s traditional script.\nWorking directly with the community showed me that contribution is not only about what I can bring, but also about what I am willing to learn. I saw how practical work could support everyday life, while cultural exchange gave me a deeper understanding of the traditions behind the community. I left Bản Sưng seeing community engagement as a two-way exchange—one where contributing and learning can happen at the same time.",
      "bodyX": 97,
      "bodyY": 224,
      "bodyWidth": 452,
      "background": "inquiry/project-background@2x.png",
