    {
      "key": "y4c",
      "route": "/community/y4c",
      "frameId": "26:24",
      "title": {
        "path": "community/type/y4c-title.svg",
        "text": "Y4C",
        "width": 128,
        "height": 58,
        "offsetX": 0.5184253454208374,
        "offsetY": 11.39999771118164,
        "artWidth": 125.0,
        "artHeight": 34.0
      },
      "titleX": 213,
      "titleY": 132,
      "body": "As a volunteer in the Youth for Community (Y4C) Program by Tiền Phong Newspaper, I joined a rural community initiative that combined practical infrastructure work with STEM education. I helped install over solar-powered streetlights, contributing to safer and more sustainable local infrastructure, while also facilitating interactive STEM sessions for 100+ children, turning scientific concepts into hands-on activities.\nWorking across both community service and education showed me how small, practical interventions can create different kinds of impact: a streetlight can change how a community uses its surroundings after dark, while an engaging STEM activity can change how a child approaches a question. The project was later featured by Tiền Phong Newspaper, highlighting the program’s community work.",
      "bodyX": 97,
      "bodyY": 224,
      "bodyWidth": 452,
      "background": "inquiry/project-background@2x.png",
