    {
      "key": "concert",
      "route": "/community/concert",
      "frameId": "26:46",
      "title": {
        "path": "community/type/concert-title.svg",
        "text": "“Viet Nam Tinh Hoa” Concert",
        "width": 883,
        "height": 58,
        "offsetX": 3.0240001678466797,
        "offsetY": 8.903998374938965,
        "artWidth": 879.0,
        "artHeight": 37.0
      },
      "titleX": 213,
      "titleY": 132,
      "body": "Traditional Vietnamese music carries stories that deserve to be heard by new generations. As a Public Relations Specialist for the Aria Project’s “Viet Nam Tinh Hoa” Concert, I worked on making those stories more accessible to younger audiences through modern cultural storytelling.\nI developed social media strategies, managed the concert’s official Facebook communications, wrote press releases, and produced promotional media assets to build interest and encourage attendance. I also coordinated promotion across channels for the free concert, helping connect its cultural message with a wider audience. Beyond communication, the project contributed to a 50,000,000 VND charity fund supporting children and youth through MSD Vietnam’s community programs.\nThis experience showed me that advocacy can take many forms. Sometimes, it means creating the space for a tradition to be seen, understood, and carried forward by people who might otherwise feel distant from it. For me, communication became a way of connecting culture, younger audiences, and community impact.",
      "bodyX": 97,
      "bodyY": 221,
      "bodyWidth": 452,
      "background": "inquiry/project-background@2x.png",
