      },
      "titleX": 213,
      "titleY": 132,
      "body": "In Mù Cang Chải, Yên Bái, the road to a classroom is sometimes a mountain trail.\nI joined Bright Paths on a journey into the highlands, carrying books, school supplies, clothes, and small things to brighten the days of over 80 local children. We learned, played, and shared stories together, discovering that cultural exchange can be just as meaningful as what we brought with us.\nAlongside the local community, we also helped install more than 10 solar lighting poles, bringing light to paths and homes after sunset.\nFor a few days, I stepped outside the familiar world I knew. I learned that making a difference does not always begin with something extraordinary. Sometimes, it begins with carrying a box up a mountain, sitting beside a child, and leaving behind a little light.",
